Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:19:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Round a sharp bend at a T vertex too: the vertex moves onto
 the arc and the ways ending there follow

A vertex another way is attached to stayed exactly where mapped, so the road
had to pass through it: an S that swings out before the vertex and turns most
of the bend within a few metres of it. On a 53 degree bend at a service road's
end (legs of 25 m and 20 m) that drew a 7.8 m radius where the arc would be
20 m, and a car on a 6 m street cut the bend into the inside kerb. Where every
other way only ends at the vertex and the bend is 30 degrees or more, the
vertex is rounded like any other (at most MAX_CUT_M inside it) and the ending
ways' ends move to the arc's middle. A way passing through the vertex, and a
gentler bend, keep the old rule.

